<title>TOGO: Bank to help Mali refurbish Timbuktu airport.</title>
<headline>Bank to help Mali refurbish Timbuktu airport.</headline>
<dateline>LOME 1997-02-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The West African Development Bank (BOAD) has agreed a 4.27 billion CFA franc loan for Mali to help it extend the runway and improve facilities at Timbuktu airport, a bank statement said.</p>
<p>The plan is to extend the runway from 1,500 metres to 2,100 metres, install radio and weather monitoring equipment and buy airport equipment and vehicles, including fire trucks, it added.</p>
<p>($1=563 CFA francs)</p>
</text>
